Thought I'd post a YAAP since this ascension represents a few
milestones, being the first in 5 years (most of those inactive in
nethack), the first on NAO and also my first healer ascension.

I think it's my 14th ascension in total.

This game's first few turns were very successful; I decided to do the
protection racket, which I have been reasonably good at with healers. I
quaffed only the healing potions straight off, in the hope of finding
some holy water before entering the mines. I found a potion of water
that I confirmed as holy on an altar on DL2. This meant I had a lot of
HP to play with while remining first level.

I needed them. Halfway to minetown, my pet died. I already had a low AC
so I decided to keep going. Engraving the E-word then running towards
the fleeing monsters seemed rather odd, but it worked well enough, and
proved worth it, as when I got to minetown I found a coaligned temple
and a tool shop with two magic lamps. Having scrounged together the
necessary holy water to bless them, I used them to get MR and
reflection, with the Eyes of the Overworld (my first ever artifact wish)
and SDSM. Soon after, I acquired a unicorn horn and I knew it would
either be ascension or YASD now.

My descent to the Castle was fairly standard. Ludios was accessible in 
this game.

I mapped Gehennom from the bottom up for the first time this ascension,
which seemed a pretty good method. I tried to use the Juiblex express,
but hit him rather too hard before he had the opportunity to teleport to
the upstairs and killed him outright. Oops.

Levitation was a bit of an issue this ascension - all I found in the
dungeon was a couple of pairs of levitation boots, one in Perseus'
statue, and one in the Castle. I used these until I was ready to wake
Rodney, then polypiled for a ring of levitation.

The Quest was a bit of a surprise as I deliberately didn't spoil myself
about it. I lost a few levels before the Cyclops went down.

I used a ring of invisibility to allow myself to toggle invisibility
until I reached the middle level of the Wizard;s tower, at which point I
couldn't see much point in being able to toggle invisibility any
longer, and zapped myself with a wand of make invisible.

I used the level teleport, cPoGL trick to get through the sanctum with
minimum fuss. Unfortunately I made the rather newbie mistake of zapping
the high priest with a /oDeath from outside the temple, and got the
"murderer" penalty. I didn't expect this to be an issue until I got to 
the sanctum, and happily a floating eye dropped a corpse in the upper
levels of the dungeon - I didn't find a tinning kit until very late in
the game. I did repair my luck with a few sacrifices on the DL2 altar
although I realised later that 11 luck might be slightly better than 13!

I used a little trick that I haven't seen specifically mentioned just
before entering the planes - I ate a huge chunk of meat to satiate
myself. This meant I was guaranteed oversatiated and in fact I ascended
still satiated despite not wearing a ring of slow digestion. In theory,
one could guarantee oneself 2900+ nutrition this way by careful eating
before entering the planes. Is there any need at all to take K-rations
to the planes I wonder?

I found quite a good method of dealing with Air Elementals. I kept
running for the portal until I was engulfed, then zapped them with a
wand of slow monster. This had the double effect of slowing them down
and expelling me. The second and subsequent times I was engulfed, I
checked if the elemental was already slow; if it was, I battered it to
death with the Staff of Aesculapius. This method seemed to prevent
drastic loss of hit points, without using up my wands of death that I
might need on Astral. As I neared the portal, I seemed to be outrunning
the remaining slowed elementals behind me. I assume this was due to them
making random moves as I was invisible, as I think they should have had
speed 24 (36*2/3) to my 20 (very fast). This meant I was able to zap a
few ahead of me with a wand of sleep.

Fire and Water didn't present any real problems.

On Astral, I located Famine at the middle altar, then blessed and
quaffed 6 potions of speed and swapped my speed boots for jumping. Once
I had outpaced my guardian angel, I put on a ring of conflict. What a
fabulous combination! After zapping Famine with a wand of death, it was
pretty easy to speed to the altar, jumping when I could and breaking
wands of teleport when surrounded.

The altar happened to be neutral, but I had brought along a helm of
opposite alignment, so I knew I wouldn't have to visit any more altars.

